<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kashkadarya</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Qashqadaryo, Kashkadarya River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kashkadarya is a river in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a> that rises in the Pamir-Alay mountains and flows west past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrisabz">Shahrisabz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qarshi">Qarshi</a> into the desert. Its fertile oases, ancient Sogdian lands, gave their name to the Qashqadaryo region of Uzbekistan. Shahrisabz, the old city of Kesh and birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>, lies in its upper valley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kashkadarya.jpg" alt="Kashkadarya" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carpodacus · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qashqadaryo_river_in_Kitab.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
